WEBVTT

00:00:00.460 --> 00:00:05.900
Infinite Ryvius

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:12.170
A new enemy?

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:15.350
No. The enemy that attacked
us at the very beginning...

00:00:15.350 --> 00:00:17.210
...has returned after making
their way around Mars' orbit.

00:00:17.210 --> 00:00:19.780
Approximately four hours before we're
estimated to be closest to them.

00:00:19.780 --> 00:00:21.580
I guess they want to
get beat up some more.

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.220
Why not fire our main
cannon against them?

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.190
What are you saying?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.880
We're using 83 percent of our support
power to sustain a gravity field.

00:00:28.330 --> 00:00:30.190
Kouji. Can you reach the Lift-ship yet?

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:32.390
Not yet. Too much static.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.100
Still no good.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:36.970
The Geduld is spreading from
where the system is damaged.

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.170
It's likely we won't be able to
communicate with them for some time.

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.400
What'll we do?

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.270
Leave things to the Vital Guarder.

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:44.560
Right. There's nothing
to be nervous about.

00:00:45.140 --> 00:00:47.940
Kouji. Leave the channel
to the Lift-ship open.

00:00:48.410 --> 00:00:49.380
Okay.

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:52.320
Hey. What's going to happen?

00:00:52.320 --> 00:00:54.580
How should I know?
Stop questioning everything.

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:58.320
We can only do what we can
and hope for the best.

00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.580
Kouji's right.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:02.890
R-Right.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:10.260
Infinite Ryvius

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:17.740
If you're going to walk, right here will be fine

00:01:18.740 --> 00:01:21.750
Although loneliness...

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:26.080
...can sometimes be unbearable

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:33.320
There's the benefit of not hurting anyone...

00:01:34.460 --> 00:01:38.400
...and the benefit of not being exposed...

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:41.360
...and hurt by others as well

00:01:41.870 --> 00:01:48.900
At the opposite side of the frozen sea...

00:01:49.670 --> 00:01:52.680
...the dream and the reality...

00:01:52.680 --> 00:01:56.300
...that you saw cross paths

00:01:56.480 --> 00:02:00.010
Some light is shed...

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:04.590
...but how it is done is unknown...

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:11.820
...so that we can go to a different place

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:19.830
The things I want have no shape

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:28.240
Tear the final universe, today until tomorrow

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:42.450
Even If I Can't Believe

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.030
We've lost contact with the Ryvius?

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:52.400
It seems to be caused by the Geduld.

00:02:52.400 --> 00:02:54.040
Battle in three hours?

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.470
Can't we return yet?

00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:57.670
Boy, I'm hungry.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.800
No use. I can barely get a word or two.
What'll we do?

00:03:03.310 --> 00:03:05.180
We know the route the Ryvius is taking.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:08.220
Right now, we'll focus solely
on what is immediately ahead!

00:03:08.220 --> 00:03:09.910
The enemy will likely
set up more mines.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:13.020
All we have to do is wipe out
the fleet, right? Not a problem!

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:14.590
It's not that simple.

00:03:14.590 --> 00:03:17.960
If we make too much noise out here,
it'll make those on Mars wary of us...

00:03:17.960 --> 00:03:19.860
...which would not be wise.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:22.560
Don't forget, we're refugees
calling out for help.

00:03:22.560 --> 00:03:23.550
I know that.

00:03:23.800 --> 00:03:24.700
Actually...

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.630
...I was really directing
that comment toward you.

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:30.870
We're counting on you.

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:33.280
Just because the Geduld
strongly influences...!

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:35.680
We can't communicate,
yet we'll be facing the enemy fleet.

00:03:36.280 --> 00:03:38.210
On top of that, we've gotta
fight while guarding the Ryvius.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:39.470
You know...

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:41.840
...I'm hungry.
Haven't you got any more food?

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:44.620
You just worry about creating
Solids in the Sub-room.

00:03:46.260 --> 00:03:47.350
How stingy!

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.450
Son!

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:51.720
Have a moment?

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:57.970
Less than three hours before we reach the
estimated closest point to our target.

00:03:57.970 --> 00:03:59.400
What's the latest on Act 32?

00:03:59.770 --> 00:04:01.830
Viatge has already established
contact with Wells Ring...

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:04.070
...and is proceeding along
the planned route.

00:04:04.310 --> 00:04:06.980
All vessels,
commence distribution of mines.

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.030
Send data to Wells Ring in real format.

00:04:14.150 --> 00:04:15.170
How'd it go?

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:17.320
It's kind of a mess up there right now.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:19.380
Are we really in a battle?

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:20.460
Looks like it.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:22.050
I can't accept that!

00:04:22.290 --> 00:04:23.960
It'll be all right.

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.830
Ikumi and the others are
battling the enemy with a robot.

00:04:26.830 --> 00:04:29.230
Also, Ikumi told me that he'd protect me.

00:04:29.460 --> 00:04:31.490
That doesn't mean we'll be safe.

00:04:31.700 --> 00:04:32.220
It does!

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:42.070
Sure it does. I believe in him.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.810
What's going on out there?

00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:46.820
I can no longer stand this.

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:48.650
Oww... That hurt.

00:04:49.480 --> 00:04:51.620
How much longer do we
have to stay on this ship?

00:04:51.620 --> 00:04:53.610
We'll be able to get off soon, okay?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:55.550
Can you really tell what's happening?

00:04:55.960 --> 00:04:57.330
They're being quite secretive
about it, aren't they?

00:04:57.330 --> 00:05:00.920
Leave it to me. In return,
I'll take all of your music chips.

00:05:04.200 --> 00:05:04.930
There!

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:07.740
Looks like we're surrounded by enemies!

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.570
You're kidding!

00:05:09.170 --> 00:05:10.570
Twelve minutes before mines reach us.

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:14.070
1 hour and 26 minutes before we reach
estimated closest point with enemy fleet.

00:05:15.180 --> 00:05:16.540
Shall we announce it to everyone?

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.770
No. It'll only cause confusion.

00:05:19.110 --> 00:05:22.240
I thought you people weren't
going to withhold any information.

00:05:22.320 --> 00:05:23.580
We're in a crisis!

00:05:23.790 --> 00:05:25.880
Are you sure the Vital
Guarder is close by?

00:05:26.590 --> 00:05:27.820
Check the radar carefully!

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:31.090
The fewest mines are in
the direction we're going.

00:05:31.490 --> 00:05:33.120
That proves that the Vital
Guarder is making a path for us.

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:35.060
Juli.

00:05:35.630 --> 00:05:36.930
Don't worry, Pat.

00:05:37.300 --> 00:05:40.890
Okay, Ryvius! Alter estimated route!

00:05:41.270 --> 00:05:42.030
I'm already doing that!

00:05:57.650 --> 00:06:00.720
Gravity field efficiency 97 percent!

00:06:00.720 --> 00:06:03.160
99.3 percent of targets destroyed!

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:04.430
Good. We can get through this!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.020
Don't let up. Concentrate.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:06.960
I know!

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:07.700
C Solid!

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:08.460
I sent it!

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:09.260
It's slow reacting.

00:06:09.260 --> 00:06:10.000
A problem?

00:06:10.000 --> 00:06:12.590
No. It's just that the mines
are now becoming wedged.

00:06:13.940 --> 00:06:16.460
Hey. Shouldn't you be supervising?

00:06:17.140 --> 00:06:19.800
They should be able to handle
this level of battle on their own.

00:06:20.140 --> 00:06:22.130
Are things all right with Blue and his gang?

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:24.700
They're probably growing
nervous as they watch us.

00:06:25.480 --> 00:06:28.140
Right now, they have no
choice but to rely on us.

00:06:29.350 --> 00:06:30.180
In other words...

00:06:30.950 --> 00:06:34.680
...the Vital Guarder possesses
all of the Ryvius' abilities.

00:06:35.290 --> 00:06:39.390
Which means right now
you and I have all the power.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:43.520
We have all the power?

00:06:46.640 --> 00:06:50.070
B-But Blue and the
others are on the ship.

00:06:50.270 --> 00:06:54.440
You see, I knew what you
guys were doing on Liebel.

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:56.810
Th-That wasn't my fault.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:00.780
I know. Besides, we can come
up with some explanation later.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:05.280
As long as we have the Vital Guarder.

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:06.790
You scoundrels.

00:07:06.790 --> 00:07:08.960
You guys aren't sharing the food.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:10.320
Gimme some.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.620
H-How dare you surprise
us like that, you brat!

00:07:25.770 --> 00:07:28.210
By the time Ryvius gets here...!

00:07:28.210 --> 00:07:30.950
Even after we account for all mines...!

00:07:30.950 --> 00:07:35.280
<i>Why's everyone dragging their feet?</i>
<i>It pisses me off! All of it!</i>

00:07:35.280 --> 00:07:36.680
I detect a ship-like shadow!

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:38.620
Enemy ship?

00:07:38.620 --> 00:07:39.920
Yeah. And it's pretty close.

00:07:40.520 --> 00:07:42.220
They're also heading
straight for the Geduld.

00:07:42.460 --> 00:07:45.430
On even ground, we have the advantage.
Send over the data!

00:07:45.660 --> 00:07:48.890
No way. When you do it, things get violent.

00:07:58.770 --> 00:08:00.340
Neutrino pinger reacting.

00:08:00.340 --> 00:08:01.980
It's our target ship.

00:08:01.980 --> 00:08:03.310
What about that other giant thing?

00:08:03.310 --> 00:08:04.250
No sign of it, sir.

00:08:04.250 --> 00:08:08.110
Transfer new target
course data to Wells Ring.

00:08:08.450 --> 00:08:10.190
Communication V, prepare to fire.

00:08:10.190 --> 00:08:12.390
Tell them to at least sink the ship.

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:16.420
Tell them any more blunders,
and they'll be laughed at across the solar
system.

00:08:16.420 --> 00:08:17.120
Yes, sir.

00:08:17.490 --> 00:08:19.860
Where could that giant thing have gone?

00:08:20.230 --> 00:08:21.250
GO!

00:08:40.550 --> 00:08:41.020
What?

00:08:51.130 --> 00:08:52.820
The fleet is changing its course.

00:08:53.260 --> 00:08:55.700
Most of them are taking a route leading
them completely away from Mars'.

00:08:55.960 --> 00:08:57.590
Wow. All in an instant.

00:08:57.970 --> 00:09:00.770
What do you think of my smart tactics?

00:09:00.770 --> 00:09:01.460
Nothing.

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.000
You could at least praise me a little, Yuki.

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:05.870
Incredible power.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:08.940
I told you. With it, we're invincible.

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:21.450
We're past the minefield.

00:09:21.920 --> 00:09:24.430
Don't let your guard down.
The fleet will be here in no time.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:25.620
Anything from the Lift-ship?

00:09:26.230 --> 00:09:27.060
Nothing yet.

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.730
Neutrino pinger reacting.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:30.900
The enemy fleet's course has been altered,
it's all over the place.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.390
Three vessels confirmed.
The rest are no longer able to pursue us.

00:09:34.000 --> 00:09:35.560
Did the Vital Guarder do that for us?

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.400
It could be a trap set up by the enemy.

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:39.170
Where is the Vital Guarder?

00:09:39.770 --> 00:09:41.000
Nothing on the pinger.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:45.440
Where could it have gone?
They know we have no attack capabilities.

00:09:46.010 --> 00:09:49.180
<i>Ikumi. Hurry up and respond.</i>

00:09:49.180 --> 00:09:51.710
<i>Kozue's waiting for you.</i>
<i>You made a promise to her, right?</i>

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:54.710
Yuki...

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:02.090
<i>What difference does that make?</i>
<i>So what if my brother's on the ship?</i>

00:10:04.530 --> 00:10:05.970
<i>What's going on with you guys?</i>

00:10:06.640 --> 00:10:07.900
<i>That bastard!</i>

00:10:09.400 --> 00:10:10.740
What in the world are you saying?

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:13.800
R-Ryvius here.
Respond, Lift-ship.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:18.010
<i>I feel the same way.</i>
<i>I don't wanna die protecting them.</i>

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:19.480
<i>But we can't do it!</i>

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:21.950
What's going on?

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:24.080
<i>But, the Ryvius...</i>

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.030
We lost transmission.

00:10:39.870 --> 00:10:42.040
Distance to target now above 30,000.

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:43.000
Main tank, blow.

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:45.870
We'll ascend while maintaining
a pace of 0. 1 herschels.

00:10:45.870 --> 00:10:47.360
At the same time, we're
switching to battle mode.

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.910
Load torpedoes!
Open all torpedo launch tubes!

00:11:04.490 --> 00:11:05.930
Infinite Ryvius

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:11.000
Infinite Ryvius

00:11:13.670 --> 00:11:14.740
Sorry to keep you...!

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:15.830
<i>What in the world are you saying?</i>

00:11:16.770 --> 00:11:19.330
<i>I feel the same way.</i>
<i>I don't wanna die protecting them.</i>

00:11:20.110 --> 00:11:21.200
<i>But we can't do it!</i>

00:11:21.610 --> 00:11:23.440
<i>But, the Ryvius...</i>

00:11:25.080 --> 00:11:26.720
That's everything we have.

00:11:26.720 --> 00:11:28.320
What's it supposed to mean?

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:30.910
The main thing we know is that the
Vital Guarder is still out there.

00:11:31.150 --> 00:11:33.020
That's wonderful news.

00:11:33.020 --> 00:11:34.280
Is Ikumi okay?

00:11:35.760 --> 00:11:36.660
Yeah.

00:11:37.160 --> 00:11:38.420
They betrayed us.

00:11:39.360 --> 00:11:41.300
What? Th-They betrayed us?

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:42.860
The Vital Guarder did?

00:11:43.160 --> 00:11:45.100
I can't believe Gran would do this!

00:11:45.570 --> 00:11:48.370
90 percent of our battle power
is with the Vital Guarder!

00:11:48.570 --> 00:11:50.370
C-Criff...

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:56.300
Son, you bastard! How could you?

00:11:56.910 --> 00:11:58.710
We don't know that yet.

00:11:58.710 --> 00:11:59.910
No.

00:11:59.910 --> 00:12:01.070
I think we can be pretty sure of it.

00:12:02.020 --> 00:12:04.050
All information we have points
to a worst-case scenario.

00:12:04.050 --> 00:12:07.110
The Ryvius has been abandoned
by the Vital Guarder.

00:12:07.520 --> 00:12:10.490
<i>If I can work at the core of this, I'm</i>
<i>confident that I can take this into flight.</i>

00:12:11.660 --> 00:12:14.180
So that's what you had in mind, Gran.

00:12:14.630 --> 00:12:15.460
That's impossible.

00:12:16.060 --> 00:12:17.400
Ikumi would never betray us!

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:20.890
There's gotta be a misunderstanding.
Yuki's there as well.

00:12:21.500 --> 00:12:23.770
It's natural to think about escaping
when in a dangerous situation.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:25.970
Besides, no one wants to die.

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:28.000
Are you saying Ikumi would betray us?

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:29.780
Ah, no, but...!

00:12:30.180 --> 00:12:32.610
How could you say such a thing?
It doesn't make sense.

00:12:33.420 --> 00:12:34.980
Generally speaking...!

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:35.720
Hey!

00:12:35.720 --> 00:12:38.690
Kouji! Would your brother really be the
type of guy who would do such a thing?

00:12:39.050 --> 00:12:41.290
To abandon his own brother so
that only he would be saved?

00:12:41.290 --> 00:12:43.350
Shut up! I'm no longer sure myself!

00:12:43.730 --> 00:12:45.220
What did you say?

00:12:46.260 --> 00:12:48.130
S-Sorry.

00:12:48.130 --> 00:12:51.220
I knew something fishy was going on.
Ignoring our orders and all.

00:12:51.870 --> 00:12:53.130
Let's come up with a plan.

00:12:53.640 --> 00:12:55.300
Considering what the
worst situation would be...

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:57.930
...we should figure out
what we can do right now.

00:12:58.140 --> 00:12:59.040
She's right.

00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.710
We can always pursue the truth afterwards.

00:13:02.010 --> 00:13:03.410
Sorry.

00:13:03.410 --> 00:13:04.840
There's no way Ikumi
would betray us, is there?

00:13:07.550 --> 00:13:08.620
What is it?

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:09.380
Enemy attack?

00:13:12.220 --> 00:13:15.790
Military data on iridium
number 32878E analyzed.

00:13:15.790 --> 00:13:18.280
The Bratica's estimated course
has been forwarded to Wells Ring.

00:13:18.430 --> 00:13:21.120
Wells Ring? I see.

00:13:21.530 --> 00:13:23.620
What is the differential to
the Bratica's present course?

00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:27.890
Phi, minus 2, xi, plus 3, gamma, zero.

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.800
We'll switch and attack portside.

00:13:30.070 --> 00:13:32.200
We'll focus our attack on
the Bratica's portside.

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:38.410
Damn Mars. They're even
using civilian facilities.

00:13:40.720 --> 00:13:43.050
How could you not have noticed
until they got this close?

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.850
Section 367 on rear
portside has been bombed.

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:48.990
Can we only wait to be destroyed?

00:13:48.990 --> 00:13:51.290
We can't attack, and we can't escape.

00:13:52.260 --> 00:13:54.130
And we have no Vital Guarder.

00:13:54.600 --> 00:13:56.360
Nothing's possible! Nothing! Nothing!

00:13:56.730 --> 00:13:58.490
We're all gonna die here.

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:00.230
No! I don't wanna die.

00:14:00.570 --> 00:14:02.370
I do not wanna die!

00:14:02.670 --> 00:14:05.400
You guys have gotta save me!

00:14:06.140 --> 00:14:07.610
Who do you think I am, anyway?

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:11.350
I am the third son of the 24th generation
of the Hojo clan, who have served...

00:14:11.350 --> 00:14:15.010
...the alliance diligently over the years,
I'm a lot nobler than you guys! Stop it!

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:19.190
I will not acknowledge such absurd
circumstances. No way! No, no, no, no!

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.310
Ryu. Throw this fool outta here!

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:25.690
What do you think you're doing?

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:28.260
I'm a Zwei and the Captain of the Ryvius...!

00:14:28.260 --> 00:14:30.660
You're no captain! You pea brain!

00:14:33.870 --> 00:14:35.500
P-Pea brain?

00:14:37.310 --> 00:14:40.400
Lucson. Please look after Pat.
You're the only one I can ask.

00:14:40.780 --> 00:14:42.580
Juli.

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:46.210
O-Okay. If you insist.

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:47.820
Juli!

00:14:47.820 --> 00:14:49.420
I'll be right there!

00:14:49.420 --> 00:14:50.510
Thanks, Lucson.

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:52.880
U-Um... Juli!

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.790
Do not worry.

00:15:02.300 --> 00:15:04.860
We Zwei members will
guarantee your safety.

00:15:05.230 --> 00:15:07.200
S-So don't cry.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:11.440
Don't cry. Got that? Don't cry!

00:15:12.140 --> 00:15:15.980
Everyone on board, I'm making an emergency
announcement from the bridge.

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:19.640
<i>Currently, Ryvius is under a
<i>torpedo attack from behind.</i></i>

00:15:20.480 --> 00:15:23.920
<i>We anticipate considerable</i>
<i>damage, so all those in portside...</i>

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:27.680
<i>...blocks 350 and above are advised to wear</i>
<i>spacesuits and evacuate to a starboard block.</i>

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.520
<i>I repeat. Currently, Ryvius is under</i>
<i>a torpedo attack from the rear.</i>

00:15:29.520 --> 00:15:30.730
What was that all about?

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:32.220
We're under attack?

00:15:34.430 --> 00:15:36.060
I hear the robot betrayed us.

00:15:36.060 --> 00:15:37.030
You're kidding!

00:15:37.030 --> 00:15:38.270
Yuki did?

00:15:38.270 --> 00:15:40.170
There's a swarm of people on
their way to the bridge again.

00:15:40.700 --> 00:15:42.200
We have no time to be dealing with them.

00:15:42.200 --> 00:15:44.470
Close all partitions connected
to the residential quarters!

00:15:49.810 --> 00:15:51.710
Those damn bridge screwballs!

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:53.580
Not again. What's wrong with them?

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:57.090
Don't we have a plan?

00:15:57.090 --> 00:15:59.050
Kreis. Send me the field.

00:15:59.490 --> 00:16:01.280
Block 378 damaged.

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:05.390
Ikumi. Hurry over. Please, hurry over!

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:07.120
Yuki.

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:09.860
<i>What's gonna happen?</i>
<i>What's gonna happen to us?</i>

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:13.030
<i>Did Ikumi really betray us?</i>

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:14.560
<i>No, I'd rather believe</i>
<i>that he would not betray us.</i>

00:16:16.300 --> 00:16:17.240
<i>What about Gran?</i>

00:16:17.240 --> 00:16:18.110
<i>And Son?</i>

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.070
<i>Akihiro.</i>

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:19.470
<i>Nicks.</i>

00:16:20.740 --> 00:16:22.000
<i>Yuki...!</i>

00:16:26.780 --> 00:16:28.080
How much longer do we have
to endure being attacked?

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.450
Let's change our course and get outta here!

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.820
<i>Hesitation and anxiety will</i>
<i>only weaken your determination.</i>

00:16:40.060 --> 00:16:41.860
I've completed a Solid
for course changes!

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:42.960
Send it over right away.

00:16:44.130 --> 00:16:45.000
No...!

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.300
I'm loading it now.
Commencing course adjustments.

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:48.470
No!

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:52.900
We mustn't change our course.

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:56.230
Even if we escape now,
we'll be under fire again in no time.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:17:00.410
And, if we stray from our course,
we won't rendezvous with the Vital Guarder.

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:06.280
We would be giving up our last
chance to survive. So... So...!

00:17:06.420 --> 00:17:08.190
Are you asking us to believe them?

00:17:08.190 --> 00:17:11.030
But we've been under attack for some time,
yet they still haven't come!

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:14.690
You don't have to
believe them. But... But...!

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.990
I'd rather place my bets where
the chance of survival is higher!

00:17:21.840 --> 00:17:23.670
Proceed along our present course!

00:17:25.810 --> 00:17:26.740
Really?

00:17:26.740 --> 00:17:27.500
Roger!

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:34.680
I knew there was something
different about you.

00:17:36.180 --> 00:17:37.670
I can't tell.

00:17:42.720 --> 00:17:43.960
We're through the Geduld.

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.150
Our radar's recovered.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:17:48.920
Submersion ship located to our rear.

00:17:49.360 --> 00:17:51.030
It's the same ship we saw
when Leibe Delta was crushed.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:51.990
Wait!

00:17:52.670 --> 00:17:54.000
There's also something
in our flight path.

00:17:54.700 --> 00:17:55.860
What is it?

00:17:56.440 --> 00:17:57.970
It's the Vital Guarder!

00:17:57.970 --> 00:18:00.380
Come on, Ikumi!
What took you so long?

00:18:00.380 --> 00:18:01.400
Really.

00:18:01.910 --> 00:18:03.540
I'm bringing up a telescopic image.

00:18:07.220 --> 00:18:08.010
What's that?

00:18:08.180 --> 00:18:11.640
A match found on our database.
It appears to be an orbital platform.

00:18:12.290 --> 00:18:13.750
Codename: Wells Ring.

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:17.190
It's a man-made satellite for transporting
goods, 20 kilometers in diameter.

00:18:17.890 --> 00:18:20.830
Goods are transported to other satellites
by utilizing the centrifugal force...

00:18:20.830 --> 00:18:23.200
...caused by the ring-shaped
mass driver and...!

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:26.100
Oh, no! If that thing's used as a weapon...!

00:18:26.300 --> 00:18:27.440
Please no!

00:18:27.440 --> 00:18:30.840
What do you mean chance to survive?
This is the absolute worst-case scenario!

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.850
Kouji! This is all your fault!

00:18:42.280 --> 00:18:44.510
They've fired at us!
It'll hit in two minutes.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:48.420
I'm detecting an object weighing a total
of 10,000 darcs, shot from Wells Ring.

00:18:48.790 --> 00:18:50.760
Moving Tandel out of the area.

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:55.030
Not yet. Continue firing at
the Bratica until we sink it.

00:18:59.900 --> 00:19:01.100
Torpedoes are also on the way.

00:19:01.100 --> 00:19:02.870
Thirty seconds to meteorite impact.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.140
I don't have enough time to
switch to the Evasion Solid.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.670
Ten more seconds.

00:19:20.250 --> 00:19:22.120
An object detected coming from
the rear at a great speed!

00:19:24.390 --> 00:19:26.380
It's passed above us.
Ship is out of control.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:27.990
Is it Vaia?

00:19:33.100 --> 00:19:33.900
Vital...!

00:19:33.900 --> 00:19:34.800
Guarder!

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.470
Retreat at once!

00:19:56.120 --> 00:19:59.720
The Vital Guarder is falling onto
Mars' surface with the meteorite.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:01.960
<i>Sorry we're late!</i>

00:20:02.300 --> 00:20:03.130
Ikumi!

00:20:03.530 --> 00:20:04.330
What took you?

00:20:04.330 --> 00:20:07.130
I apologize. I'll explain...!

00:20:25.690 --> 00:20:27.020
Let go of the meteorite!

00:20:27.020 --> 00:20:28.650
I know that!

00:20:34.000 --> 00:20:35.400
Where's the Vital Guarder?

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:37.160
Wha...? Look...

00:20:50.040 --> 00:20:51.840
I think we just arrived in hell.

00:20:54.050 --> 00:20:58.280
But I'm amazed that Ryvius
remained on its planned course.

00:20:59.320 --> 00:21:01.050
You read it perfectly.

00:21:05.590 --> 00:21:08.990
It doesn't really matter...
who suggested it.

00:21:14.270 --> 00:21:15.630
Explain what happened, Ikumi!

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:17.430
We had a traitor on board.

00:21:21.240 --> 00:21:27.370
P-Please forgive me. I was tricked by Gran.
It was all planned by him.

00:21:27.720 --> 00:21:29.650
He's the one at fault here!

00:21:30.220 --> 00:21:31.180
Liar.

00:21:31.350 --> 00:21:34.380
You were acting awfully snobbish,
saying you're invincible and all.

00:21:34.590 --> 00:21:40.620
I told you, he tricked me. Help me.
Forgive me. We're friends, right?

00:21:41.100 --> 00:21:44.390
Friends? I have no idea what
you're talking about.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:50.570
H-Help me, please. Help. No! Don't!

00:21:50.870 --> 00:21:53.340
Please don't! I apologize!

00:21:58.510 --> 00:22:06.940
NOOO!!!

00:22:07.740 --> 00:22:12.010
In your dry eyes...

00:22:12.010 --> 00:22:17.090
...a silhouette appears

00:22:17.090 --> 00:22:21.790
The blue colored future...

00:22:21.790 --> 00:22:28.520
...swayed and glittered

00:22:29.700 --> 00:22:37.940
Ah... No one wants...

00:22:37.940 --> 00:22:46.550
...freedom out of pity

00:22:46.550 --> 00:22:54.990
Ah... To the days I feared...

00:22:54.990 --> 00:22:58.890
...that I'd end up hurting someone,

00:22:58.890 --> 00:23:05.260
goodbye

00:23:09.290 --> 00:23:11.120
Infinite Ryvius

00:23:11.120 --> 00:23:11.420
Infinite Ryvius
Next episode: After the Party

00:23:11.420 --> 00:23:14.290
Next episode: After the Party
A party is thrown in celebration.

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:18.560
Next episode: After the Party
And new facts are disclosed,
after the party.

00:23:18.560 --> 00:23:20.730
Next episode: After the Party
There are those who meet,
those who quarrel...

00:23:20.730 --> 00:23:22.400
Next episode: After the Party
...those who touch
one another's feelings.

00:23:22.400 --> 00:23:24.600
Next episode: After the Party
We know nothing lasts forever.

00:23:24.600 --> 00:23:26.410
Next episode: After the Party
That's exactly why
we want to shout it out.

00:23:26.410 --> 00:23:27.770
Next episode: After the Party
I wish time would stop.

00:23:27.770 --> 00:23:29.540
Next episode: After the Party
Please, stop!
